WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.180
Artificial intelligence is altering
research methodologies across all

2
00:00:04.220 --> 00:00:06.200
scientific and academic domains.

3
00:00:07.080 --> 00:00:11.040
Historically, research evaluation functioned
as a static pre-approval process.

4
00:00:11.300 --> 00:00:15.040
A committee reviewed a fixed proposal,
granted clearance, and the project

5
00:00:15.080 --> 00:00:17.900
proceeded under specific, unchanging
parameters.

6
00:00:18.280 --> 00:00:20.200
Machine learning changes that logic.

7
00:00:20.460 --> 00:00:24.120
Because these algorithms adapt to new data
parameters during deployment,

8
00:00:24.280 --> 00:00:27.340
a single point-in-time oversight is no
longer sufficient.

9
00:00:27.520 --> 00:00:29.940
For institutional oversight bodies, the
goal has shifted.

10
00:00:29.980 --> 00:00:34.020
they must establish rigorous, dynamic
frameworks capable of performing

11
00:00:34.060 --> 00:00:38.460
continuous evaluation. Using AI in
research creates a new operating

12
00:00:38.500 --> 00:00:42.860
environment. Managing it requires a
structural evolution in how we assign and

13
00:00:42.900 --> 00:00:44.740
maintain ethical responsibility.

14
00:00:45.140 --> 00:00:48.540
This shift means ethical oversight must
now map directly to the actual

15
00:00:48.580 --> 00:00:50.112
timeline of software development.
